---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy — KeeForge" description="KeeForge does not collect your vault data. The optional in-app feedback form only sends the message you choose to submit, plus visible error details when reporting a database-open failure.">
    <div class="privacy">
        <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to KeeForge</a>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: April 22, 2026</p>

        <div class="content">
            <p class="lead">KeeForge does not collect your vault data. The optional in-app feedback form only sends the message you choose to submit, plus visible error details when reporting a database-open failure.</p>

            <h2>No Analytics</h2>
            <p>KeeForge contains no analytics frameworks, no crash reporting SDKs, and no usage tracking of any kind.</p>

            <h2>No Telemetry</h2>
            <p>KeeForge does not make background network requests. The only outbound connections the app ever makes are: (1) to the cloud storage providers you explicitly configure (iCloud Drive, Dropbox, OneDrive, etc.) to sync your database files, and (2) a single request to our feedback endpoint when <em>you</em> tap &ldquo;Send&rdquo; in the in-app feedback form (see below).</p>

            <h2>No Accounts</h2>
            <p>KeeForge does not require or offer account creation. There is nothing to sign up for.</p>

            <h2>Your Vault Data</h2>
            <p>Your passwords, entries, attachments, and master password stay on your device and in your own cloud storage. KeeForge has no ability to read, access, or transmit your vault data to anyone. The app operates entirely offline except for the file syncing you choose to enable and the opt-in feedback submissions described below.</p>

            <h2>Feedback Submissions</h2>
            <p>KeeForge includes an in-app feedback form (available from Settings and from certain error screens). The form is entirely optional &mdash; the app's features and services do not depend on using it. When, and only when, you tap &ldquo;Send,&rdquo; the app submits the following information to our feedback endpoint at <code>https://feedback.keeforge.com/api/feedback</code> over HTTPS:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>The free-text message you typed.</li>
                <li>If you were sending feedback from a database-open error screen: the visible error details shown in the app, such as the error category, error code, title, summary, and technical details. These contain no entries, passwords, key files, raw vault files, or other vault contents.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The app does not automatically attach app version, build number, iOS version, device model, or separate follow-up contact fields. If you choose to type personal information into the message itself, that text is sent because you included it manually.</p>
            <p>We use this information solely to read your feedback and diagnose bugs. We do not use it for advertising, profiling, or analytics, and we do not sell it. Submissions are stored on infrastructure operated on our behalf by our hosting provider; any such provider is contractually required to protect the data to the same standard described in this policy and to process it only on our instructions.</p>
            <p>We retain feedback submissions for up to 24 months so we can review related reports, and then delete them. You can request deletion of a feedback submission at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:support@keeforge.com">support@keeforge.com</a> or by opening an issue on <a href="https://github.com/crazytan/KeeForge">GitHub</a>. You can also simply decline to use the feedback form &mdash; if you never tap &ldquo;Send,&rdquo; nothing is transmitted.</p>

            <h2>Children</h2>
            <p>KeeForge is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect information from children through the feedback form.</p>

            <h2>Open Source</h2>
            <p>Don't take our word for it. KeeForge is open source under the GPLv3 license. You can <a href="https://github.com/crazytan/KeeForge">audit the code yourself</a>, including the exact fields the feedback form sends.</p>

            <h2>Changes To This Policy</h2>
            <p>If we change what the app collects or how we use it, we will update this page and change the &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date above before the change ships in a public build.</p>

            <h2>Contact</h2>
            <p>If you have questions about this policy, email <a href="mailto:support@keeforge.com">support@keeforge.com</a> or open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/crazytan/KeeForge">GitHub</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</Base>

<style>
    .privacy {
        max-width: 640px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 60px 24px 80px;
    }

    .back-link {
        display: inline-block;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        color: var(--text-dim);
        margin-bottom: 40px;
        transition: color 0.2s;
    }

    .back-link:hover {
        color: var(--text);
    }

    h1 {
        font-size: 2.4rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
        background: none;
        -webkit-text-fill-color: var(--text);
    }

    .updated {
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        color: var(--text-dim);
        margin-bottom: 40px;
    }

    .content {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 24px;
    }

    .lead {
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--green);
        padding-bottom: 24px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    h2 {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-bottom: -16px;
    }

    p {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: var(--text-dim);
    }

    @media (max-width: 480px) {
        .privacy {
            padding: 40px 20px 60px;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 1.8rem;
        }
    }
</style>
